Subject: [PATCH 1/2] scratch: tail_3 upper mean bound (screen, never pushed)

Tail3UpperBoundConfig(coef, bound, index=14), tail3_upper_bound_penalty
(mean over rows of relu(mu[:, 14] - b)^2) and enable_tail3_upper_bound in
mirror_kl_ppo.py, off by default. The term is added in _mirror_loss after
kappa * L_K (a separate forward pass with gradient when coef > 0; at coef 0
the hook's no-grad mean is only logged, nothing is added), so train() and
train_source_diff are unchanged. train/tail3_bound_* telemetry per update.
The bound's state is excluded from the checkpoint; only the JSON record
mesozoic_tail3_bound is saved, and a bound zip loads with stock PPO.

