T1a and T1b compared no bound with coef 0 only on the toy's default
action_net.bias[14], where mu14 sits far below both b and L_B is 0 on every
row, so a coef-0 branch that added any multiple of the penalty passed.
Both now also run the comparison with bias[14] = 1.0 and = b in BOTH
models (rows above b) and assert the coef-0 model's logged penalty and
beyond fraction are positive there while the gradient sequence (T1a) and
the digests (T1b) stay byte-equal. A mutation that makes the coef-0 branch
add 2.7 or 0.37 x the penalty now fails T1a at both b.

